WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:03.349
This slide lets us see how UNKNOWN behaves when
combined with TRUE

00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:08.895
and FALSE For example TRUE AND UNKNOWN becomes
UNKNOWN because we

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:12.479
do not know whether the missing side would have been
true FALSE

00:00:12.505 --> 00:00:16.255
AND UNKNOWN becomes FALSE because one false
condition is already enough to

00:00:16.281 --> 00:00:21.126
make the entire AND expression false TRUE OR UNKNOWN
becomes TRUE because

00:00:21.152 --> 00:00:26.344
one true condition is enough At the bottom we have a
runnable

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:31.513
example that creates combinations of TRUE FALSE and
UNKNOWN Run it in

00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:36.236
the browser and inspect the output table If you want
to study

00:00:36.262 --> 00:00:40.102
the behavior more closely copy the query into
pgAdmin and run it

00:00:40.128 --> 00:00:45.941
there You do not need to memorize every combination
immediately Focus

00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:49.549
on understanding why SQL sometimes cannot make a
definite decision
